  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nFrom https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/280\n\n> When data has been entered or modified in a form it is convenient to notify the users that they will lose the data if they leave the page without having submitted the form. Currently, to do this, it is necessary to use Javascript to monitor the changes, monitor when the user avandonates the page with the \"beforeunload\" event and display a warning message. This could be easily done by the browser if it is indicated in a parameter of the form.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nAdding a custom `beforeunload` which does `confirm('Some message') && preventDefault()`\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nA simpler attribute which the browser can provide some useful default messages.\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
